course: dictionary
lesson: 1040
title: Words on the edge
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some things sit on a line between two groups, so it is hard to say which group they belong to. Borderline means only just on one side of that line. A borderline pass is a mark right at the pass mark: it passes, but only just.
explain: «A borderline case is an example on the edge of a group, like whether a hot dog is a sandwich.» Nobody is quite sure, so the case sits on the border. Silly cases like this train careful thinking, because you have to say why something belongs in a group and why it does not.
explain: Words can be borderline too. «A few words are borderline: "méi jiàoyǎng" (badly brought up) blames a child's whole family, and "lǎowài" (foreigner) is casual and mostly harmless, but some people don't like being labelled.» The context shows that these words are not clearly rude or clearly fine: they sit on the edge.
fact: Borderline means only just on one side of a line between two groups or results.
fact: «A borderline pass» is a mark right at the pass mark, so the teacher must decide.
fact: As a noun, a borderline is a line that marks a border.
fact: In medicine, borderline means close to being an illness or problem but not quite, as in «borderline high blood pressure».
fact: A good check is to ask: does this clearly fit the group, or does it sit on the edge?
exercise: The teacher said his mark was borderline. What does this mean? | It was a clear fail | It was the highest mark in the class | *It was only just a pass, so the teacher had to decide | It was written in pencil
exercise: «Is a hot dog a sandwich? It is a borderline case.» What does borderline case mean here? | A case that is clearly a sandwich | A case about a border between two countries | *An example on the edge of a group, hard to put in one or the other | A hot dog with no bread
exercise: In «A borderline case is an example on the edge of a group», which word is closest in meaning to borderline? | case | group | *edge | example
test: «The result was borderline, so the judge had to think carefully.» What does borderline suggest? | *Hard to decide which side it is on | Clearly the winner | Written in capital letters | Shown on a map
test: Which sentence uses borderline as a noun? | The result was a borderline win | That joke is borderline rude | The test was borderline easy | *The fence marks the borderline between the two farms
exam: Mia says her spelling test was borderline. What is the best meaning? | *Only just on one side of a line, so it is hard to call pass or fail | Hard to read because of the border around the page | Very easy and fun | Longer than all the others
